Me:

I am using Drafter to make my website. I have buttons for sorting resorts, filtering by snow conditions, and viewing individual resort details. I am confused about how the buttons communicate with the different functions in my program. I also have a State dataclass. Can you explain what the state is doing and how the buttons connect to the routes?

ChatGPT:

In Drafter, the state keeps track of information that needs to be remembered as the user moves between pages.

For your project, you have several useful state variables:

resorts stores the resort information.

selected_resort keeps track of which resort the user selected.

sort_mode remembers how the resorts should be organized.

good_snow_only keeps track of whether the snow filter is active.

When you create a button, you give it a route name. That route name should match a function decorated with @route.

When the user clicks the button, Drafter runs the corresponding route function. That function can update the state and return a new page.

For example, clicking the closest resorts button could change the sorting mode in the state and then rebuild the homepage.

For the View Details button, you can also pass the selected resort's ID as an argument so the details page knows which resort to display.
